    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the existing patterns and a maintainer of this codebase would find it natural:\n\n- `formatSalutation` is placed among the other `format*(Owner)` derivation methods in `OwnerMapper`, mirrors their exact shape (null-guard returning `null`, same Javadoc style), and reuses the same `title == null || title.trim().isEmpty()` blank-check idiom already used in `composeAddress`. It's the right unit for this derived, read-only DTO field.\n- The `@Mapping(target = \"salutation\", ...)` entry sits alongside the sibling expression mappings in `toOwnerDto`, consistent with `displayName`, `initials`, etc.\n- `Owner.title` with its getter/setter is a plain JPA field following the surrounding convention, and the `title` column is added uniformly across all four schema dialects (h2/hsqldb/mysql/postgres).\n- The OpenAPI additions (request `title` with the `MR|MRS|MS|DR` pattern, read-only response `salutation`) match the documentation style of neighboring properties.\n\nNo duplication, no catch-all growth beyond the mapper's established role as the home for these derived-field formatters, and logic lives where the other derivations already live.",
